  "worked_solution": "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \u27e820{t}^{3},\\,16t({t}^{2}-1)\u27e9\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \u27e820{t}^{3},\\,16t({t}^{2}-1)\u27e9\\text{d}t & =\u27e8\\int 20{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 16t({t}^{2}-1)\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e85{t}^{4}+{c}_{1},\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+{c}_{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=\u27e81,\\,5\u27e9$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=\u27e85\\cdot {1}^{4}+{c}_{1},\\,4{({1}^{2}-1)}^{2}+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e81,\\,5\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e85+{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e81,\\,5\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-4$ and ${c}_{2}=5.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=\u27e85{t}^{4}-4,\\,4{({t}^{2}-1)}^{2}+5\u27e9.\n$$",
